  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Schools and organisers value clear records and follow-up. They judge you by accuracy, tidy writing and useful next steps.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is noting facts as they happen.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and report on career guidance programme: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools help tidy language and format tables. Routine formatting shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Accuracy, consent and judgment about what matters hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to polish wording and check facts yourself; later, own the programme design.
  </p>

